# Next.js App Router

## Route groups

| Group | Path | Purpose |
|-------|------|---------|
| `(store)` | `/`, `/shop`, `/checkout` | Public storefront |
| `(dashboard)` | `/admin/*` | Admin panel |
| `(info)` | `/about/*` | Static info / legal pages |
| `(auth)` | `/login`, `/register` | Auth flows inside store layout |

## Server vs client components

- **Default to Server Components** in `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx` when there is no client state, effects, or event handlers.
- Add `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, `useState`, browser APIs, contexts).
- Extract client UI into `*Client.tsx` or colocated components (e.g. `ShopPageClient.tsx`, `AdminLayoutClient.tsx`).

## Metadata

Use helpers from `@/lib/seo`:

```typescript
import { pageMetadata, noIndexMetadata, aboutPageMetadata } from "@/lib/seo";

export const metadata = pageMetadata({ title: "Tienda", description: "..." });
// Admin, checkout, account → noIndexMetadata()
// About pages → aboutPageMetadata("slug")
```

## Data fetching

- Server pages: fetch in the page or in `src/lib/*` loaders (e.g. `loadProductPageData`).
- Client lists/filters: fetch in client components via `@/lib/catalog` or `@/lib/api`.
- Do not duplicate API URL logic — always go through `@/lib/api`.
